.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-list - List enrolled machines


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List enrolled machines

.PP
Show enrolled machines and their current account-visible state. Use the returned machine identity for rename, capabilities, availability, or revoke.

.PP
Machines are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected machine, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
